        "date": "2026-11-12T13:53:00Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): hold an undeclared post script to the lathe door on a lathe or mill-turn\n\nA user's own turning script with no `capabilities` line was read as a\nmill post, so the #1190 door did not fire and a milling pass could post\nwith the work spindle at the cutter's rpm. `post::dialect::declared_turning`\nnow tells \"declared not turning\" from \"undeclared\", and\n`lathe_voice::at_post` holds an undeclared script to the door for every\noperation whose setup mounts a machine with a work spindle (lathe,\nmill-turn), naming the missing manifest line and the fix. Declared\nscripts and every other machine behave as before; no shipped post or\ngolden changes.\n\nFixes #1199\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
